SUMMARY:Mercy Hawkins: Waltz of Life & Limb
DESCRIPTION:Mercy Hawkins: Waltz of Life & Limb\nExhibit: October 3 – November 6\, 2026\nReception: October 9\, 6-9 PM (Free) \nWaltz of Life & Limb pairs recent sculptural paintings by artist Mercy Hawkins\, with her vibrant\, large-scale watercolors on paper. With this work\, Hawkins seeks to answer the internal call\, to encounter what the body already knows\, from our own inner rhythms\, heartbeat\, and breath\, to dancing with wild arms. Her biomorphic shapes\, formed of intersecting dots\, dashes\, and lines\, speak to a sensory play of color\, light\, and movement. Her imagery evokes seed pods\, flower buds\, or microscopic creatures\, immersing the viewer in an all-encompassing perception of nature. \nArtist Talk: Saturday\, October 17\, 2-3:30 PM (Free)\nMercy Hawkins will speak about the development and trajectory of several bodies of recent work\, including its connection to craft. She will also explore the intersection of painting and music. \nSponsored by HF Richardson \nImage: Mercy Hawkins\, “Melting Ice”
URL:https://thedirt.online/event/mercy-hawkins-waltz-of-life-limb/
LOCATION:Pence Gallery\, 212 D Street\, Davis\, CA\, 95616\, United States
CATEGORIES:Art
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://thedirt.online/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Mercy-Hawkins-Melting-Ice-scaled.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Pence Gallery":MAILTO:pencegallery@gmail.com
END:VEVENT
